 present paper introduces a repeated,
 generated N-of-1 trial on type systems:
 the experiment generates multiple code fragments that can be tested on one participant and then repeated on multiple participants.
 I.e.,
 instead of a realistic scenario,
 the experiment uses generated source code in a very restrictive but very focused way.
 In the present study this leads to an experiment where two factors were studied but where the data collection on a single participant required on average less than 5 minutes.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
More precisely,
 
\end_layout

