\begin_layout Standard
Taking a look into the discussed works,
 it is plausible to us that developers have doubts about existing studies.
 While we found 14 experiments in the literature,
 only three detected a positive effect of static types (two further studies detected positive effect of static types on at least one dependent variable),
 while two detected a positive effect of dynamic types.
 Taking additional studies on type annotations into account reveals a comparable picture (3 studies,
 one pro type annotations,
 one contra type annotations).
 From this rather vague picture it is plausible to start with replications of such experiments.
 But the experiments in the literature are expensive–authors report experiment time per participant between 24.7 minutes and 27 hours.
 Furthermore all experiments are designed in a way that multiple participants are necessary–and the total experimentation times vary between 33 hours and 1,323 hours.
