\begin_layout Standard
One might argue that controlled experiments are rather not adequate to compare programming languages features (especially not type systems) because of the high costs.
 However,
 in case it is possible to reduce such costs,
 controlled experiments can help to identify factors influencing the effect of language features in general,
 respectively type systems in particular.
 Hence,
 our goal was to define a controlled experiment with relatively small costs.
