The absence of the four non-conform participants leads also to a slightly different perspective on the results of individual participants.
 Without non-conform participants,
 there are two participants (both PhD students) among the remaining 18,
 who did no longer reveal an effect of the main variable type system (
\begin_inset Formula $\frac{2}{18}=11\%$
\end_inset

),
 which means that the status is only approaching significance towards the likelihood to show an effect of the main variable (
\begin_inset Formula $\chi²$
\end_inset

(1,
 N = 18) = 3.54,
 p = .060,
 see Table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
